{"absent":["Architectural implementations behind the arch-specific 64-bit primitives and the generic exchange and compare-exchange helpers are not shown.","Exact memory-ordering semantics of the full, acquire, release and relaxed fences beyond their placement are not shown.","Full type layouts, sizes, alignment and initialization rules for the 32-bit and 64-bit atomic containers are not shown.","Effects, ordering and failure modes of the checking hooks for read, write, combined access and barrier markers are not shown.","Locking rules, futex behavior, interrupt or preemption constraints, and progress guarantees of retry loops are not shown."],"dossier":"D03","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot_relaxed"],"text":"Raw 64-bit layer offers masked-clear fetch operations with acquire, release and relaxed ordering that atomically clear a caller-chosen bit set and report the value seen before the change."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_or","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_or","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_or_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_or_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_or_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xor","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_xor","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_xor_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_xor_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_xor_relaxed"],"text":"Raw 64-bit layer offers bitwise OR and XOR updates as non-reporting stores plus prior-value-reporting fetch forms covering full, acquire, release and relaxed ordering."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_cmpxchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_cmpxchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_cmpxchg_relaxed"],"text":"Raw 64-bit layer offers unconditional exchange and three-way compare exchange, each in full, acquire, release and relaxed ordering, reporting prior content and storing conditionally only on expected match for the latter."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_try_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_try_cmpxchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_try_cmpxchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_try_cmpxchg_relaxed"],"text":"Raw 64-bit layer offers boolean compare exchange in all four orderings that consumes an expected-value pointer and a replacement, stores only on equality, refreshes the caller expectation when the comparison fails, and signals success as a boolean."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_not_zero","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_unless_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_unless_positive","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_if_positive"],"text":"Raw 64-bit layer offers result-test helpers reporting zero after subtract, decrement or increment and negativity after add, plus guarded arithmetic that adds or steps only when current content avoids a forbidden value or sign and returns prior content, computed result, or success indication."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_set_release"],"text":"Instrumented 32-bit layer exposes acquire read and plain plus release store accessors that validate the access and then delegate to the matching raw accessor."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_sub_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_sub_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_sub_return_relaxed","includ