.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_xor","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_try_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative"],"text":"When an architecture lacks a directly ordered primitive, full ordering is assembled from the relaxed form bracketed by full fences, acquire by relaxed work followed by an acquire fence, and release by a release fence followed by relaxed work; a natively ordered arch form is preferred when present."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_fetch_andnot_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_sub_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_dec_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_negative_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_inc_not_zero"],"text":"Derived operations reuse simpler ones: masked-clear uses masked-clear-set with an inverted mask, zero tests compare a returning arithmetic result against zero, negativity tests compare a returning add against less than zero, plain guarded add compares a prior-value guarded add against its guard, and nonzero-guarded increment is a guarded add of one against zero."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_set_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_add_return_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_fetch_add_relaxed"],"text":"Instrumented wrappers validate before delegating: reads use a read hook, stores a write hook, and read-modify-write operations a combined hook; full-order returning forms also record a full barrier marker and release forms a release marker, while acquire, relaxed and non-reporting forms record no barrier marker."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::_LINUX_ATOMIC_INSTRUMENTED_H"],"text":"The instrumented header defines a multiple-inclusion guard macro."},{"kind":"struct","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_xchg_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_cmpxchg_relaxed"],"text":"A 64-bit atomic value is held in a container exposing a 64-bit integer member that generic exchange and compare-exchange fallbacks address directly."},{"kind":"state_machine","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_try_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic64_try_cmpxchg_relaxed"